From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikhail Mlhcnn <mikhail@advnirr.org>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 13:58:30 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] panvk/csf: give compute jobs the TLS size of the shared
 allocation

Command buffers use a shared TLS allocation sized for the largest stack
requirement. Compute and precomp dispatches copy the base pointer into
their private TSD, but previously left the TLS size field set to the
job's own shader stack size.

With packed TLS addressing, thread stack stride depends on this size field.
When jobs with different stack sizes execute concurrently without barriers,
the job with smaller stride overwrites the stack of the other job, causing
memory corruption or out-of-bounds GPU page faults.

Fix this by copying word 0 (TLS size) of the shared descriptor along with
the base pointer.

Fixes GPU page faults in 3DMark Wild Life Extreme on Mali-G615.

Fixes: 5544d39f442 ("panvk: Add a CSF backend for panvk_queue/cmd_buffer")
Fixes: cc02c5deb42 ("panvk: Implement precomp dispatch")
Assisted-by: Claude Code (Claude Opus 5.5)
Reviewed-by: Lars-Ivar Hesselberg Simonsen <lars-ivar.simonsen@arm.com>
Reviewed-by: Boris Brezillon <boris.brezillon@collabora.com>
Reviewed-by: Erik Faye-Lund <erik.faye-lund@collabora.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/44753>
(cherry picked from commit 09ad390c8d06b73289228a43de572b5c5797c4a7)

[rg477m: partial backport on the RC5-universal base. The panvk_vX_cmd_precomp.c
hunk is left out: with it, upstream's gpu_prerast tessellation kernels (libpan
precomp, dispatched next to prerast compute jobs that keep their own TLS size)
write bad records, PanProbe large_draw tess_tri_direct/indirect fail every
run; without it they pass. App compute dispatches keep the fix.]

Purpose: partial backport of Mesa main 81db71cf (the app-dispatch half; the precomp hunk is left out on the RC5-universal base, where it breaks upstream gpu_prerast tessellation kernels: PanProbe large_draw tess_tri fails every run with it): compute and precomp jobs copy the shared TLS base pointer but kept their own (smaller) stack size, so with packed TLS addressing concurrently running jobs with different stack sizes overwrite each other's stacks (GPU page faults, e.g. 3DMark Wild Life Extreme on Mali-G615)
Upstream-commit: 81db71cf (Mesa main, MR 44753), partial; when the pinned Mesa base includes it, check that large_draw still passes
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: none of ours
Validation test: on RC5-universal-110: PanProbe large_draw PASS with this hunk only, FAIL (tess_tri_direct/indirect) with the full backport, PASS on plain upstream; earlier (RC3 base, full backport): PanProbe 38/38, drawbench 8/8, racetest and msrtss identical to rg477m/016
Generated-by: upstream (backport with git am; precomp hunk removed by rg477m)
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_dispatch.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_dispatch.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_dispatch.c
index 3586e17b..5985d99a 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_dispatch.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/csf/panvk_vX_cmd_dispatch.c
@@ -410,11 +410,13 @@ cmd_dispatch(struct panvk_cmd_buffer *cmdbuf, struct panvk_dispatch_info *info)
 
    struct cs_builder *b = panvk_get_cs_builder(cmdbuf, PANVK_SUBQUEUE_COMPUTE);
 
-   /* Copy the global TLS pointer to the per-job TSD. */
+   /* Copy the global TLS pointer and size to the per-job TSD. */
    if (cs->info.tls_size) {
       cs_move64_to(b, cs_scratch_reg64(b, 0), cmdbuf->state.tls.desc.gpu);
+      cs_load32_to(b, cs_scratch_reg32(b, 4), cs_scratch_reg64(b, 0), 0);
       cs_load64_to(b, cs_scratch_reg64(b, 2), cs_scratch_reg64(b, 0), 8);
       cs_move64_to(b, cs_scratch_reg64(b, 0), tsd);
+      cs_store32(b, cs_scratch_reg32(b, 4), cs_scratch_reg64(b, 0), 0);
       cs_store64(b, cs_scratch_reg64(b, 2), cs_scratch_reg64(b, 0), 8);
       cs_flush_stores(b);
    }
